    "surfaces": "Invert each archived cover STL registration. Invert the production generator’s axial-end print rotation and centering with its installed fine-model bounds. The receiver fixtures and production back-top STL share machine coordinates.",
    "caps": "Boolean differences between the entire production and trial print solids, in mm³. The two values are production-only and trial-only volume. The Pisco trial has three recessed identification dots on the cover back. Production fills those marks.",
    "receivers": "Intersect each print solid with the listed installed XYZ box, enclosing both cheeks, their ends and the fitted hardware passage in the working span. Compare the volumes in both directions. An exterior panel strip beyond the ASSE working span carries the full part’s print flutes. The Pisco fixture has three further exterior ID dots on its flange.",
    "sections": "Section both sides at 11 equally spaced axial positions, from 0.03 mm inside the fore end to 0.03 mm inside the aft end. Compare both directions across the contour of each leaf from root to foot, and across its fixed cheek from the approach through the stop. Distances are maxima of the densified section-edge Hausdorff distances in mm.",
    "viewer": "The installed assembly references the current source payload digest. Decode each of its four immutable cap assets and compare its position, normal, triangle-index and face-range buffers byte for byte against the matching body of the current installed cover set. All four use identity placement. The back-top node references the same asset as the current quadrant."
  },
